# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Two purposes, and the second one is a security boundary rather than an
# optimization:
#
# 1. Keep the build context small.
# 2. Ensure evaluation truth and development artifacts never enter the image.
#
# `lib/reports.ts` reads its Markdown from 03_Sample_Data/ with a path Next's
# file tracer cannot resolve statically, so the tracer conservatively marks the
# WHOLE directory as required. A standalone build would therefore copy
# Ground_Truth.jsonl into the runtime image even though no product code imports
# it. Excluding it here means it never enters the build context at all, which is
# a stronger guarantee than deleting it from the image afterwards.
#
# The four Report_*.md files are deliberately NOT excluded: `next build`
# prerenders `/` and reads them at build time.

# version control
.git
.gitignore

# build output and dependencies (rebuilt inside the image)
.next
node_modules
coverage

# BUILD-9 evaluation harness — never reachable from product runtime
eval

# product documentation and decision records
01_Product_Brief
04_Eval
05_Product_Decisions
08_Build_Log

# evaluation truth and non-runtime sample data
03_Sample_Data/Ground_Truth.jsonl
03_Sample_Data/PDF
03_Sample_Data/Sample_Report_Spec.md

# secrets and local environment
.env
.env.*

# local artifacts and noise
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
**/.DS_Store
